<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56396" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κειμήλι-ον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεῖμαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything stored up as valuable, treasure, heirloom</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆ νῦν, καὶ σοὶ τοῦτο, γέρον, κ.
					ἔστω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.618
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Xenoph.
				2.9
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρον . . ὅ τοι κ. ἔσται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.312
				</span></i>
			; 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀφνειοῦ πατρὸς κ. κεῖται, χαλκός τε
					χρυσός τε πολύκμητός τε σίδηρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.47
				</span></i>
			; opp. live chattels (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόβασις</span>),
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.75
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				438
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				591
			</span></i>; of a person, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				654
			</span></i>; of a fish, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. Ἀμφιτρίτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					21.55
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐσθλά</span>. of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνῶμαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				362.4
			</span></i>: rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Prom.Es</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PGiss.</u>
				35.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλος ἀνυπόστατον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Secund.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			; in bad sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακὸν κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Lex</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>relic</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅγια κ. τῆς ἐκκλησίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PGrenf.</u>
					2.111.1
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(v/vi A.D.)</span>.</div>
